! C22-6578 PROBLEM 3.10, "INTEGER PART OF Log2N", printed p.34 (PDF 35),
! read in the ink.
!
!   "N is a positive floating number in DOG, and log2N can be written
!   as an integer plus a positive fraction.  Find the integer and put
!   its magnitude in the first 18-bits of the value field of $1, and
!   the sign in the sign position of the value field of $1.  Assume no
!   exponent flag."
!   Analysis: N = 2**alpha * beta, 1/2 <= beta < 1, so log2 N =
!   (alpha - 1) + (1 + log2 beta) with 0 <= 1 + log2 beta < 1, and
!   "alpha - 1 expressed as an 18-bit VFL integer, is the desired
!   quantity."
!
!   Method 1.   L(N), DOG
!               E-I, 1
!               L(B, 12, 1), 8.0, 6
!               ST(B, 25, 1), $1
!               BEW, $
!
! The five printed statements are the deck's last five before its data,
! as printed.  Blocks A and B are the same four instructions on other
! data with DOG renamed (the pattern of problem_3_2.strap).  Each block
! is preceded by the deck's own LX, $1, PAT, which fills $1 with a
! pattern so that a store reaching past the value field would show, and
! blocks A and B are followed by the deck's own SX to keep what $1 held.
! The page gives no DOG; the deck's are below.
!
! ASSEMBLED WITH ASM=strap2 (see problem_3_1.strap).
!
! WHAT EACH STATEMENT DOES, with the page of the rule:
!   L(N), DOG: a normalized load, so the exponent is alpha.
!   E-I, 1: no dds, so (U) (C22-6578 printed p.30, comment (c)); the
!     exponent becomes alpha - 1.
!   L(B, 12, 1), 8.0, 6: a VFL load of the 12-bit field at address 8.0.
!     That field is accumulator bits 0-11: the exponent flag, the ten
!     exponent bits, and the exponent sign.  Reference Manual printed
!     p.61, LOAD: "The numeric part of the addressed operand is placed
!     in the accumulator as specified by the offset.  The sign bit in
!     the sign byte register is set according to the sign of the data";
!     and of the byte size in a binary operation (p.61, ADD TO MEMORY,
!     "Radix", which LOAD shares through ADD): "the byte size refers only
!     to the length of the sign byte, thereby determining the position
!     of the sign bit".  A one-bit sign byte makes bit 11, the exponent
!     sign, the sign, and bits 0-10 (the flag, zero by the page's
!     assumption, and the magnitude) the number.  The offset of 6 puts
!     the number's units bit six places in from the accumulator's right
!     end (problem_3_2.strap's header: offset 68 is bit 59), so the
!     accumulator holds (alpha - 1) x 64.
!   ST(B, 25, 1), $1: 25 bits to word 17 bits 0-24, the value field of
!     $1 (Reference Manual printed p.23, LOAD VALUE: "The value field,
!     bits 0-24, of the index word").  A one-bit sign byte again: bits
!     0-23 the number, bit 24 its sign.  (alpha - 1) x 64 in 24 bits is
!     alpha - 1 in bits 0-17 with bits 18-23 zero -- "the first
!     18-bits".  Bits 25-63 of $1 are not touched.
!
! THE EXPECTED VALUES ARE HAND-DERIVED.  PAT is A5A5A5A5A5A5A5A5; its
! bits 25-63 (00000025A5A5A5A5 of the word) survive.  The magnitude
! lands at bits 0-17 (shift 46), the sign at bit 24 (8000000000 of the
! word).
!     block  N      alpha  log2 N      alpha - 1   $1 afterwards
!     A      8      4      3           +3          0000C025A5A5A5A5
!     B      3/16   -2     -2.415      -3          0000C0A5A5A5A5A5
!     last   1000   10     9.966       +9          00024025A5A5A5A5
!   (8 = .1 x 2**4; 3/16 = .11 x 2**-2; 1000 = .1111101 x 2**10.)
!   PC 87: the printed BEW is the right half of word 43 in the host
!   STRAP II's assembly (the VFL L and ST before it are full words),
!   half-word 87.
!   Block A is an exact power of two, where the page's "positive
!   fraction" is zero; block B is N below 1, the negative sign.
!
! INJECTION, OBSERVED 2026-11-16 (data side, on a copy of the deck, the
! deck itself untouched): DOGA changed from 8 to 7.  FAIL A_value only
! (got 00008025A5A5A5A5, alpha - 1 = 2); B_value, the last block's $1
! and the PC passed.

START   LX, $1, PAT
        L(N), DOGA
        E-I, 1
        L(B, 12, 1), 8.0, 6
        ST(B, 25, 1), $1
        SX, $1, RESA
        LX, $1, PAT
        L(N), DOGB
        E-I, 1
        L(B, 12, 1), 8.0, 6
        ST(B, 25, 1), $1
        SX, $1, RESB
        LX, $1, PAT
! --- the page, as printed -------------------------------------------
        L(N), DOG
        E-I, 1
        L(B, 12, 1), 8.0, 6
        ST(B, 25, 1), $1
        BEW, $
! --- the deck's data ------------------------------------------------
DOG     DD(N), 1000
DOGA    DD(N), 8
DOGB    DD(N), 3/16
PAT     DD(BU, 64), 11936128518282651045
RESA    DR(BU, 64), (1)
RESB    DR(BU, 64), (1)
        END, START
